RNG

This distribution provides pseudorandom number generators and documents the
provider interface used by Perl's C<${^RNG}> variable. The generators are
intended for
simulations, testing, and other non-cryptographic uses. RNG::PCG is a small
XS implementation of Melissa O'Neill's two-dimensional PCG-XSH-RR generator.
RNG::Drand48 exposes Perl's built-in drand48-compatible generator through the
same interface, primarily for comparison and compatibility testing.
RNG::Wyrand and RNG::Xoshiro are additional fast XS generators for
non-cryptographic use.
RNG::HMAC_DRBG is an XS HMAC-SHA-256 provider following the HMAC_DRBG
construction in NIST SP 800-90A; it offers deterministic and operating-system
seeded modes, but is not FIPS validated.

See the module documentation for details.
